<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Colmán Már</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 555</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Colman Mor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Colmán Már was a 6th-century Irish dynast of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a>, a son of the high king Diarmait mac Cerbaill. He was the ancestor of Clann Cholmáin, which by the 8th century became the dominant line of the kings of Mide and supplied several high kings of Ireland, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mael-sechnaill-mac-maele-ruanaid">Máel Sechnaill mac Máele Ruanaid</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mael-sechnaill-mac-domnaill">Máel Sechnaill mac Domnaill</a>.</p></div>
